LC 380 — Insert Delete GetRandom O(1)
Pattern:Hashing + Array

Logic:
vector → stores values
unordered_map → stores value → index
This lets insert, delete, and random access work in O(1).

Algorithm:
Insert → add to vector + map
Remove → swap with last + remove
GetRandom → random vector element


CODE:
class RandomizedSet {
    vector<int> v;
    unordered_map<int,int> mp;

public:
    bool insert(int x) {
        if (mp.count(x)) return false;
        mp[x] = v.size();
        v.push_back(x);
        return true;
    }

    bool remove(int x) {
        if (!mp.count(x)) return false;
        int i = mp[x];
        v[i] = v.back();
        mp[v[i]] = i;
        v.pop_back();
        mp.erase(x);
        return true;
    }

EX:
We start with:

[10, 20, 30]

Want to remove 20.

Instead of shifting everything, take the last element 30:

[10, 20, 30]
     ↓
replace 20 with 30

[10, 30, 30]

Then remove the last element:

[10, 30]

Now:

GetRandom()

can return either:

10 🎲
or
30 🎲

👉 Why swap with last?
Because removing the last element from a vector is O(1).

    int getRandom() {
        return v[rand() % v.size()];
    }
};
Complexity:

Insert: O(1) average
Remove: O(1) average
GetRandom: O(1)
